| `make gate-baseline` `[tree,write]` | Runs, in a generated project, the gate test of every check `scripts/expiring_tier_data.py` `CHECKS` registers through `scripts/record_gate_baseline.py`, and rewrites `expiring_tier.baseline` with the project's own findings, stamped with `.copier-answers.yml` `_commit`. Run it once after `copier update`, because until it runs a gate test that adopts the tier is red naming it. The configured output is confined to the project; escapes exit 14 before checks run. | `make gate-baseline` | [`expiring_tier.baseline`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`expiring_tier.expires`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`PY`](settings.md#make-variables) | Writes the tree, and its recipe opens with `$(WRITE_GUARD)`, so CI and a Ralph loop cannot grow the file. At an unchanged `_commit` it refuses any new entry and writes nothing. Exits 2 in the template repository, which has no tier. It does not stop a hand edit of the file: review holds that. | [generate-and-upgrade.md](../guides/generate-and-upgrade.md) | always |
